From: Eric Berquist <eric.berquist@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] python313Packages.aiormq: 9.6.4 -> 6.9.4, fix version metadata

aiormq has never released a 9.6.4.  Upstream pushed two tags on
2026-03-22, 6.9.4 and 9.6.4, and they point at the same commit
(c1ba6e80404b88f2be174479a15d89f5ceba6a03) -- 9.6.4 is a
transposed-digit duplicate.  Sorting tags numerically picks the bogus
one, which is presumably how it landed here.

The src hash is unchanged, because the two tags are the same tree.

That commit also still declares `version = "6.9.2"` in pyproject.toml:
upstream tagged the release without bumping it.  So the build fails even
once the tag is corrected --

    The 'aiormq' derivation has version '6.9.4' but .dist-info/METADATA
    specifies version '6.9.2'.

-- and pyprojectVersionPatchHook resolves that, as the error message
itself recommends.

Correcting the version is not cosmetic.  aio-pika, the only reverse
dependency in nixpkgs, requires `aiormq<7,>=6.8`, so patching the
metadata while leaving version at 9.6.4 merely moves the failure one
package downstream:

    Checking runtime dependencies for aio_pika-9.6.0-py3-none-any.whl
      - aiormq<7,>=6.8 not satisfied by version 9.6.4

That bound is also why this stays on 6.x rather than moving to the newer
7.0.0, which is self-consistent but outside aio-pika's range.

Without this, python3Packages.aiormq does not build at all, taking
aio-pika and everything downstream of it with it.

---
diff --git a/pkgs/development/python-modules/aiormq/default.nix b/pkgs/development/python-modules/aiormq/default.nix
index 31e7a30..f8bc86a 100644
--- a/pkgs/development/python-modules/aiormq/default.nix
+++ b/pkgs/development/python-modules/aiormq/default.nix
@@ -3,13 +3,14 @@
   buildPythonPackage,
   fetchFromGitHub,
   pamqp,
+  pyprojectVersionPatchHook,
   uv-build,
   yarl,
 }:
 
 buildPythonPackage rec {
   pname = "aiormq";
-  version = "9.6.4";
+  version = "6.9.4";
   pyproject = true;
 
   src = fetchFromGitHub {
@@ -26,7 +27,10 @@ buildPythonPackage rec {
 
   pythonRelaxDeps = [ "pamqp" ];
 
-  build-system = [ uv-build ];
+  build-system = [
+    pyprojectVersionPatchHook
+    uv-build
+  ];
 
   dependencies = [
     pamqp
